{
  // THE SINKS - DESIGN-SINKS.md. What the Armory sells for Valor and the Archive sells for Coda.
  //
  // NOT PART OF ContentDatabase.ContentVersion, on purpose, for guild-path.json's reason: nothing
  // here is read by a fight. Retuning a price must not retire every guild's replays.
  // ContentDatabase.LoadSinks reads it after Load. The whole shop is behind SinksSwitch and
  // stays dark with it off, whatever this file says.
  //
  // PRICES ARE DAYS OF INCOME, never currency amounts. One day of income is what a player at the
  // highest Proving standing (or Recital floor) reached earns in a day of full attempt banks;
  // SinkPricing turns days into Valor or Coda and rounds up to priceRound. A fixed amount would be
  // generous in week one and worthless by week ten, and days scale by themselves.
  //
  // NOTHING HERE IS RANDOM. kind is a closed set: armor (a fixed preset, built by hand), brand
  // (+1 Proving attempt), echo (+1 Recital attempt), heroCopy (+1 copy of a hero the player picks
  // from the list). An unknown kind is dropped with a warning. The shops sell for earned currency
  // only.
  //
  // cap: items that share a cap key share one counter. per is "day" (the reward day, 04:00 UTC)
  // or "month" (the calendar month of the reward day).
  //
  // armor presets are Honed at most (ArmorInfo.MaxDropTemper). primary is the slot's guaranteed
  // stat, at its Honed magnitude. LoadSinks drops a preset whose values fall outside armor.json's
  // ranges, so a preset can never be better than a roll could have been.
  //
  // heroes lists are explicit ids, four star heroes only, never a starting hero, and no hero in
  // two lists. A roster addition never changes a shop silently.
  "priceRound": 5,
  "items": [
    { "id": "armory_weapon", "shop": "armory", "kind": "armor", "days": 6,
      "cap": { "key": "armor", "per": "month", "limit": 3 },
